    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/3951822": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. Purpose of Role FIN 300 Investment Markets (3 credits) This course will present students with real world exposure to investing in 3 major markets; the stock market; the real estate markets, and the franchise market. Students will learn about wise investment strategies by participating in a stock market simulation, developing a real estate investment plan and identifying a franchise opportunity that aligns with their interest and values. Guest speakers from these industries will enhance the instructor's presentation with real world examples and experiences. Three adjuncts will co-teach this course during the semester $1166 per course. Daemen University strongly encourages all campus community members to get vaccinated for COVID-19, including a booster vaccine."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/4177645": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. Purpose of Role Pre-Teaching Assistant Instructor in Behavioral Science Department, Daemen University Daemen University is seeking applications for a Pre-Teaching Assistant Instructor position in the Behavioral Science Department. The purpose of this position is to provide a volunteer in the role of a Teaching Assistant with education and training in teaching and instructional skills in the field of behavior analysis. This will also allow the individual an opportunity to gain valuable experience in teaching at the graduate level in order to obtain future teaching opportunities. This individual will serve in a Pre-Teaching Assistant role to a faculty member in the Department of Behavioral Science. Pre-TA Activities Under the mentorship of the course instructor, the Pre-TA will learn skills that bridge theory and online instructional delivery in a practice-based manner, including observing course structure and instructor-student interactions. Instructor-student interactions can be synchronous, through student support groups, and asynchronous, such as emails that are specific to course learning. Responsibility of the Pre-TA The Pre-TA may facilitate asynchronous discussion boards, provide targeted feedback on low-stakes assignments, and support small-group or individual student engagement through messaging or virtual office hours under the supervision of the primary instructor. Additional responsibilities may include monitoring student participation, assisting with course organization and content accessibility, and engaging in structured reflection (e.g., weekly journals) to analyze effective online teaching practices. Supervision of the Pre-TA The Pre-TA operates under full-time faculty supervision with clearly defined responsibilities aligned to course objectives and student needs, with the goal of developing competencies in online pedagogy, instructional communication, and learner support while exploring teaching as a professional pathway. Operational considerations Participation requires access to key institutional systems (e.g., the learning management system, communication platforms, and grading tools) and adherence to Daemen University's employee engagement and compliance requirements. Qualifications required : The Pre-TA will have a Masters Degree in Behavior Analysis or related field and/or the equivalent coursework (e.g., BCBA qualifying program completion). Board Certified Behavior Analyst and Licensed Behavior Analyst in NY or the state in which they practice in good standing is preferred. PhD in Training requirements for the Pre-TA FERPA Cultural Sensitivity Training- to be completed by the department Sexual Harassment Training LMS Training- to be completed by the department Other Background Check (to be completed by Employee Engagement) Reference Checks (to be completed by the academic department) This position is not compensated, strictly voluntary Faculty mentorship is not compensated, strictly voluntary Application Process and timeline (TBD) by the academic department) The mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly complex world. Daemen University is an independent, nonsectarian, comprehensive university located in Amherst, a first ring suburb of Buffalo, New York. For consideration, apply directly at https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/ and upload your CV, letter of interest, and contact information for three professional references. Daemen University is an AA/EOE and strongly encourages applications from women, veterans, people of color, individuals with disabilities, and candidates who will contribute to and support the cultural fluency and diversity of our campus. Review of applicants begins immediately and continues until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/3795269": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Anatomy &amp; Physiology",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Anatomy &amp; Physiology. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. Purpose of Role The Department of Natural Sciences is seeking an Adjunct instructor for our introductory Anatomy and Physiology Lecture course. A bout This Opportunity The Adjunct instructor will be responsible for teaching an introductory course in Anatomy & Physiology (BIO 207) designed primarily for first-year students in the Nursing major. The lecture meets for 1 hour and 20 minutes twice a week and is coupled with a 1 credit laboratory that meets once a week to be taught by a separate instructor. It is one part of a two-semester sequence. The student learning objectives are as follows: 1) acquire and use the language of anatomy and physiology, 2) understand the levels of organization of the human body, 3) understand organ systems, and their components, processes, and functions, 4) have a thorough enough understanding of these principles that you may apply them to human behavior, health, physiology, and pathology in the future. Knowledge and Skills: -Experience with & active learning; in both an online and face to face modality -Demonstrate analytical and organizational skills necessary to plan, implement and evaluate educational activities to assure compliance with established goals and objectives -Demonstrate strong interpersonal and communication skills, verbal and written, necessary to interact effectively with all university constituents -Strong time management/organizational skills -Demonstrated commitment to working with diverse populations $2,800 - $3,000 per semester Required Qualifications -Candidate should possess a master's degree or higher in an appropriate field, have experience that relates to the course material and facility with the online environment. Previous teaching experience is preferred. Daemen University strongly encourages all campus community members to get vaccinated for COVID-19, including a booster vaccine."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/3909105": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Health Promotion",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Health Promotion. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. Purpose of Role Part-time adjunct instructor role to teach Health Promotion coursework in the areas of: Community Health Education, Administration (health care management and policy), and Fitness related coursework. HPR 350 Fitness Testing and Programming $2550.00 per contract Required Qualifications Master's degree in related field, especially Community or Public Health, Health Administration or Exercise Science/Fitness Related; previous experience teaching college-level coursework preferred Daemen University strongly encourages all campus community members to get vaccinated for COVID-19, including a booster vaccine."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/3828074": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Pool Social Work &amp; Sociology",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Pool Social Work &amp; Sociology. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. Purpose of Role The Daemen University Social Work and Sociology Department Program invites applications for part-time adjunct faculty positions to teach undergraduate- and graduate-level social work courses. Adjunct instructors are needed to teach in a variety of content areas across the MSW curriculum, including generalist and advanced social work practice, human behavior in the social environment, social policy, and research methods. Opportunities to provide elective courses on various populations, issues, or treatment modalities, as well as supervision to students in field practicums are also available. Courses may be offered in-person, online, or in hybrid formats, depending on department needs. About This Opportunity Joining our Social Work & Sociology team, the Adjunct Faculty Positions will be responsible for the following: Deliver high-quality instruction in alignment with Council on Social Work Education (CSWE) competencies and program learning outcomes; Deliver course content in accordance with provided master syllabi and departmental standards; Facilitate class discussions, experiential learning activities, and student engagement; Maintain regular communication with students and respond to inquiries within a reasonable timeframe; Identify students in need of academic and/or other supports; Evaluate and provide timely, constructive feedback on student performance; Submit grades and required documentation in accordance with university policies; and Collaborate with administrators and faculty to ensure academic consistency and quality . $3000 per course for Undergraduate Faculty $3500 per course for Graduate Faculty Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Master of Social Work (MSW) degree from a CSWE-accredited program Minimum of two years post-MSW professional experience Demonstrated expertise in one or more areas of social work education Commitment to culturally responsive, anti-racist, anti-oppressive, and evidence-informed teaching practices Excellent communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills Preferred Qualifications: Licensure (LMSW, LCSW) in applicable jurisdiction Doctorate in social work or a related field (e.g., DSW, PhD) Prior teaching experience in higher education, particularly in graduate-level social work programs Experience with online teaching and learning platforms (e.g., Canvas, Blackboard, Zoom) Experience with diverse student populations including first generation students a plus Compensation: Adjunct faculty are compensated on a per-course basis, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Daemen University strongly encourages all campus community members to get vaccinated for COVID-19, including a booster vaccine."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/4116516": {
      "title": "Adjunct Income Tax Accounting Instructor",
      "description": "Adjunct Income Tax Accounting Instructor. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. Purpose of Role Adjunct Income Tax Accounting instructor for Fall 2026 semester. Class is scheduled for Tuesdays and Thursdays, beginning on Tues Sept 8th and concluding by Thurs Dec 17th. Course objectives are to instruct students to prepare individual tax returns including appropriate supplemental schedules, use a tax software package to prepare tax returns electronically, and apply basic tax planning procedures. The class concludes with IRS Volunteer Income Tax Assistance training. Specific areas of coverage include: tax formula, tax determination, gross income, exclusions, deductions and losses, itemized deductions, investor losses, and property transactions. Class is currently slated for 2:30 - 3:50 on Tues/Thurs, however, could be rescheduled to begin later in 80 minute blocks on Tues/Thurs or possibly just one 2-hour-forty-minute block on Tues."
    },
