    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/4189459": {
      "title": "ASCEND Program Coordinator",
      "description": "ASCEND Program Coordinator. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. Purpose of Role The ASCEND Program at Daemen University is seeking a compassionate, organized, and student-centered Part-Time Program Coordinator to support its Comprehensive Transition and Postsecondary (CTP) program for students with intellectual and developmental disabilities (IDD). This innovative program offers students the opportunity to audit university courses, participate in campus life, and develop career readiness and independent living skills in a supportive environment. About This Role The Program Coordinator will support the day-to-day operations of the ASCEND Program, playing a key role in ensuring its success. Responsibilities include collaborating with faculty and staff, supporting students in academic and social settings, coordinating inclusive campus engagement, and facilitating vocational experiences. This role requires a strong commitment to inclusion, excellent communication and organizational skills, and a passion for empowering students with IDD to reach their goals. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Program Coordination & Management Coordinate student schedules, course audit plans, and academic modifications in collaboration with faculty and supports provided through Accessibility Services. Support program within the campus community, including academic departments and student life. Manage program resources, such as expenses and materials. Student Support & Progress Monitoring Provide individualized support and planning for students. Coordinate access to academic supports such as assistive technology and tutoring. Monitor student progress and maintain accurate documentation and reports. Lead student workshops on soft skills, job readiness, independent living, and campus navigation. Career Development Support students iCAP (Career Action Plan) activities, workshops, and portfolio development. Coordinate job-shadowing, internships, and on-campus work experiences that align with student goals. Maintain communication with local businesses and community organizations to expand and support employment opportunities. Community Engagement & Communication Facilitate ongoing communication among students, peer mentors, families, and campus community. Assist with planning and participate in program events, orientation, outreach, and recruitment activities. Represent the program at community events and campus-wide initiatives. Peer Mentor & Staff Training Oversee, train, and support peer mentors and interns who work alongside ASCEND students. Assist in supporting and providing resources to faculty, staff, and mentors on inclusive education practices. Stay current with emerging research and best practices in the field of inclusive postsecondary education. Required Qualifications The ideal candidate will have the following background, credentials, and/or characteristics: A bachelor's degree in Education, Special Education, Disability Studies, Rehabilitation Counseling, Social Work, or a related field. Experience working with individuals with intellectual disabilities and their families in special education and/or related agency settings, including but not limited to teaching, counseling, program coordination, administration within K-12 or postsecondary education institutions. Strong communication, organizational, interpersonal, and administrative skills. Ability to work both independently and as part of a collaborative team with diverse groups of people. Excellent communication skills for engaging with students, families, faculty, staff, and external partners. The ability to advocate for inclusive practices, promote awareness of disability issues, and build community support is critical. Preferred: Experience in higher education, school-based, or postsecondary transition programs. Knowledge of person-centered planning, universal design for learning (UDL), or vocational rehabilitation services."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/4034482": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. Purpose of Role Daemen University seeks applications for one (1) full-time, tenure-track teaching position in its Social Work and Sociology Department. The successful candidate will teach Clinical Social Work Practice courses (Advanced Clinical Practice, Clinical Practice with Children and Adolescents) and/or elective courses focusing on populations, conditions, or intervention strategies. Courses may be taught in person or hybrid on the Amherst (Main) Campus or via Distance Education (Online). This is a twelve (12) month appointment. About This Opportunity Joining our Social Work and Sociology team, the Assistant Professor will be responsible for the following: Conduct assigned classes in keeping with standards established by Social Work & Sociology faculty and administration in consultation with the Academic Dean and Provost; Assess proficiency of teaching and accomplishments of students in assigned courses at regular and timely intervals; Provide advisement to diverse students in preparation for graduation, future academic pursuits, and/or professional social work practice; Mentor students in completion of service/research projects, independent studies, and other scholarly activities; Assist in the on-going design, implementation, and evaluation of the Social Work & Sociology curriculum; Keep abreast of field of study/profession by reading current scholarship and attending relevant professional development training and/or conferences; Provide evidence of an active and productive research agenda; Engage in service through participation with the Institute for Government and Non-Profit Innovation, Training, and Evaluation (IGNITE), field education supervision, or other; Perform committee work within the Social Work & Sociology Department and Daemen University including re-accreditation related activities; Assist in marketing, communications, and student recruitment for the Social Work & Sociology Department and Daemen University; Attend meetings called by the Daemen University President, Provost, Academic Dean, Department Chair, and/or MSW Program Director; and Perform other duties as requested and/or required in accordance with the Daemen University Faculty Handbook Required Qualifications Possess a Master of Social Work (MSW) degree from a CSWE-Accredited College or University Minimum: Two-years post-MSW experience Minimum: Two (2) years teaching experience at the undergraduate and/or graduate level Be credentialed as a Licensed Clinical Social Worker (LCSW) in New York or other jurisdiction or willing to pursue, transfer, or renew licensure. A doctoral degree in Social Welfare or related disciplines is strongly desired. Candidates will be considered if they can provide evidence demonstrating they are on a path to timely degree completion. Total Compensation Daemen University offers a robust total compensation package that includes: Health insurance with an option of two plans: an HSA plan with the deductible funded by employer HSA contributions, or a copay plan. Dental insurance through the Guardian network. Vision insurance through the Guardian network, and an option between the VSP or Davis plans. An 8% employer contribution to the retirement savings account when employees contribute just 5%. Fully paid long term disability insurance, guaranteed-issue life insurance for new hires up to a volume of $150,000. Tuition waiver for full-time employees and their qualified dependents. Entrance in Tuition Exchange scholarship opportunities to pursue education at other institutions. Generous time off for administrative and staff employees. Daemen University strongly encourages all campus community members to get vaccinated for COVID-19, including a booster vaccine."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/4229180": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Practice. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. About This Opportunity The Criminal Justice Program at Daemen University is searching for a full-time, non-tenure tack, Assistant Professor of Practice. This individual will help to lead, strengthen, and further develop this new, fast-growing program. Criminal Justice is an interdisciplinary program that ensures graduates will be well prepared for careers in criminal justice professions, while receiving a strong liberal arts education that provides them with a deeper understanding of political, psychological, and social environments. The ideal candidate will have a mix of applied experience in the criminal justice field and a demonstrated ability to teach at the undergraduate level. This non-tenure track position carries teaching responsibilities equivalent to 24 credit hours across the two-semester academic year. The successful candidate will also be expected to develop co-curricular programming and to provide student advisement and mentoring. The position reports to the Chairs of History & Political Science and Psychological Sciences, as co-directors of the program. Required Qualifications Daemen University invites applications for a full-time, 9-month, non-tenure track faculty position in the Criminal Justice Program starting on 25 January 2027. Applicants must have, at minimum: A Master's degree in Criminal Justice or a closely related field; Experience teaching at the college level (including the ability to teach Criminology, Policing and Corrections, Criminal Justice Theory, and the Capstone experience); Relevant practical experience and a willingness to work with students in securing meaningful internships; A willingness to plan programming to engage students on campus or in the community in experiential learning opportunities. The ideal candidate will also would also possess the following Additional Qualifications: A PhD in Criminal Justice or a related field A demonstrated ability to publish in peer-reviewed publications, or experience supervising student research projects. Applications should include a cover letter of application, statement of teaching philosophy including evidence of teaching effectiveness (if available), curriculum vitae, and three letters of recommendation. We welcome you to visit our department's website for more information at: https://www.daemen.edu/academics/college-arts-sciences-education/history-political-science/criminal-justice-bs Total Compensation Daemen University offers a robust total compensation package that includes: Health insurance with an option of two plans: an HSA plan with the deductible funded by employer HSA contributions, or a copay plan. Dental insurance through the Guardian network. Vision insurance through the Guardian network, and an option between the VSP or Davis plans. An 8% employer contribution to the retirement savings account when employees contribute just 5%. Fully paid long term disability insurance and guaranteed-issue life insurance for new hires up to a volume of $150,000. Tuition waiver for full-time employees and their qualified dependents. Entrance in Tuition Exchange scholarship opportunities to pursue education at other institutions."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/4140805": {
      "title": "Assistant Strength &amp; Conditioning Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Strength &amp; Conditioning Coach. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. About this Opportunity Contribute to the educational mission of the University by coordinating the instruction of student-athletes in the area of strength & conditioning; Assist in planning workouts, conducting workouts, and supervising use of equipment. Provides motivation and support for the student-athletes; Monitor effectiveness of strength and conditioning programs and activities of intercollegiate varsity athletics in collaboration with the Head Strength and Conditioning Coach, Sports Medicine staff and sport coaches. Follow best-practice industry standards and guidelines regarding exercise technique, prescription, progression, and tolerance utilizing all appropriate and available safety mechanisms. Assist in educating sport coaches and student-athletes on flexibility, strength and conditioning and sport-specific functional programming to prevent injuries and optimize sports performance. Assist Head Strength and Conditioning/Sports Performance Coach with maintaining accurate and up-to-date training records and team / individual strength and conditioning programs via a file system and or subscription-based electronic software package (e.g. TrainHeroic). Follow established emergency action plans for the University's athletic facilities. Operates the program under the rules and regulations of the College, the NCAA, and the ECC. Assist in ensuring all fitness and sports performance equipment are functioning properly. Assist in providing suggested strength and conditioning information to Daemen University community, including information on proper use of athletic conditioning equipment as needed. Maintains professional credentials by engaging in professional development and satisfying continuing educational requirements set forth by the respective credentialing body (e.g. National Strength and Conditioning Association (NSCA) or Collegiate Strength and Conditioning Coaches Association (CSCCa)) and or the New York State Education Department (NYSED) as needed. Performs other duties as assigned by the Head Coach. Required Qualifications Bachelors degree in Exercise Science, Health or Human Performance or related field Masters degree and previous collegiate sports performance experience preferred Strong time management, interpersonal, organizational, written and oral communication skills. Be able to apply a 'team' approach to the delivery of student-athletic health care. Must be able to work long periods under conditions requiring moderate physical demands. Ability to work early mornings, evenings, weekends, and some holidays when necessary. Valid driver's license required. License must meet insurance company rules and regulation for driving underwriting criteria. Previous experience coaching at a high level. Knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations. Valid driver's license required. License must meet insurance company rules and regulations for driving underwriting criteria. Possess and maintain a national strength and conditioning certification that meets the NCAA legislation. Examples include: National Strength and Conditioning Association (NSCA) - Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist (CSCS) Collegiate Strength and Conditioning Coaches Association (CSCCA) - Strength and Conditioning Coach Certified (SCCC) -or- Master Strength and Conditioning Coach (MSCC) Adhere to established professional ethics / conduct codes as outlined by the specific professional strength and conditioning certification organization: CSCCA - Code of Conduct NSCA - Professional Code of Ethics Maintain certification in Basic Life Support level CPR/ AED."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/3812542": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. About This Opportunity Within the Scott Bieler College of Health Professions, Daemen University offers an entry level Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) degree program. The DPT curriculum is a 6 year, 3+3 program. Students may apply to the Bachelor of Science in Natural Science/DPT program as freshmen or transfers. Students already possessing a baccalaureate degree may apply directly to the professional phase of the curriculum. The Physical Therapy Department is currently comprised of 12 highly motivated core faculty members engaged in a variety of clinical, service, and scholarly activities with a common goal of providing an outstanding educational experience for our students. Programs and activities are available to mentor junior faculty in pedagogy and scholarship. External clinical practice opportunities exist locally across all clinical practice settings. Daemen University provides a dynamic academic environment that fosters strong collaborative and inter-professional efforts within the University and local medical community. Our Scott Bieler College of Health Professions building provides state of the art lecture and laboratory facilities dedicated for our PT students in all clinical practice settings. In Fall 2020, we opened the Center for Interprofessional Learning and Simulation and just recently expanded the footprint to include a simulated ICU hospital room that includes a high-fidelity manikin and 10 point-of-care ultrasound units. Standardized patients are also regularly utilized across numerous courses in our curriculum. In the spring of 2025, we opened a state-of-the-art rehabilitation facility - the Kennedy Institute for Mobility Innovation & Technology - that will offer access to leading robotic devices and assistive technology to restore motion and function following a range of injuries and illnesses. This center will become Western New York's most comprehensive advanced rehabilitation facility of its kind in the region. Required Qualifications Daemen University invites applications for a full-time, 12-month, tenure track faculty position in the Physical Therapy Department starting on 08 September 2026. The preferred candidate for this position would have expertise in neuromuscular physical therapy. In addition, the preferred candidate will have completed their academic doctorate (e.g., PhD, EdD, DHSc) in physical therapy or a related field, hold an advanced specialty certification (e.g., PCS, NCS, GCS) and be eligible for PT licensure in New York State. Candidates may be considered if they are near completion of their academic doctorate. Candidates without an academic doctorate who have a DPT degree and advanced specialty certification (as noted above) may also be considered. Previous teaching experience and evidence of scholarship are strongly preferred. Contingent upon expertise and interest, additional teaching opportunities may include neurobiology and prosthetics/orthotics, as well as mentoring students in patient care experiences on-campus and in clinical research. Non-teaching responsibilities would include student academic advising, participating in departmental and university-wide committees, clinical practice, and ongoing scholarly productivity within a related field. Opportunities for internal funding to establish and strengthen research projects are available on a competitive basis. Applications should include a cover letter of application, statement of teaching philosophy, curriculum vitae, and three references with contact information. We welcome you to visit our department's website for more information at: http://www.daemen.edu/academics/areas-study/physical-therapy Total Compensation Daemen University offers a robust total compensation package that includes: Health insurance with an option of two plans: an HSA plan with the deductible funded by employer HSA contributions, or a copay plan. Dental insurance through the Guardian network. Vision insurance through the Guardian network, and an option between the VSP or Davis plans. An 8% employer contribution to the retirement savings account when employees contribute just 5%. Fully paid long term disability insurance, guaranteed-issue life insurance for new hires up to a volume of $150,000. Tuition waiver for full-time employees and their qualified dependents. Entrance in Tuition Exchange scholarship opportunities to pursue education at other institutions. Generous time off for administrative and staff employees. Daemen University strongly encourages all campus community members to get vaccinated for COVID-19, including a booster vaccine."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/4163653": {
      "title": "CC Light Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "CC Light Adjunct Instructor. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. Purpose of Role ANIM 421 Advanced Lighting: This course will instruct students in the advanced lighting techniques needed to light their CG capstone films. Qualifications Candidate must have an excellent understanding of CG lighting techniques in Maya. Also knowledge of transferring and manipulating the rendered layers in NUKE. BFA in Animation a must. Qualifications Masters' degree required, ABD/Ph.D.preferred. Prior experience teaching undergraduate students required, with either teaching experience in an equivalent course or courses with similar content."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/4163575": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Academic Support and Engagement",
      "description": "Coordinator, Academic Support and Engagement. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. Purpose of Role The Coordinator provides operational support for the Office of AS&E, including assisting with the implementation of student success initiatives, including academic coaching About This Opportunity Assist with the day-to-day administration and operations of academic coaching serving approximately 80-125 academic coaches each semester. Support with hiring, training, and onboarding new and returning academic coaches by coordinating communications, timelines, employment documentation, and compliance requirements. Assist with the academic coach payroll process, including reviewing payroll punches against session documentation forms, identifying discrepancies, and appropriate follow-up communication where needed. Assist with maintaining accurate academic coach and program records, databases, tracking systems, and operational documentation. Develop and facilitate student success workshops and educational programs. Serve as a communication liaison with faculty regarding Academic Coaching referrals. Promote academic coach growth through communication, resources, and professional development opportunities. Collaborate with faculty and other campus partners to develop and coordinate initiatives that promote student success, engagement, persistence, and academic confidence. Oversee and contribute to social media content marketing AS&E services, workshops, resources, and initiatives. Contribute to assessment efforts including preparing reports on Academic Coaching participation and utilization. Promote inclusive, student-centered programming that responds to student needs. Support the Director of AS&E with program initiatives, projects, and operational needs as needed. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree required; Master's degree in Higher Education Administration or a related field preferred Minimum three years experience in higher education, or related field Demonstrated commitment to supporting students' academic growth, success, and overall development. Possess an enthusiastic and positive attitude. Maintain confidentiality in a discreet and professional manner. Strong writing and oral presentation skills are necessary. Effective and friendly communication skills with a variety of students, staff, faculty, and administrators. Proficient computer skills and experience with Google workspace. Demonstrates cultural awareness and the ability to support students from diverse backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives Self starter, skilled at and open to exploring ways to improve current systems. Execution focused Detail and accuracy oriented. A work schedule that will primarily include daytime hours, with occasional evening commitments and nontraditional hours during onboarding Position is full time, ten month, hourly (non-exempt). Total Compensation Daemen University offers a robust total compensation package that includes: Health insurance with an option of two plans: an HSA plan with the deductible funded by employer HSA contributions, or a copay plan. Dental insurance through the Guardian network. Vision insurance through the Guardian network, and an option between the VSP or Davis plans. An 8% employer contribution to the retirement savings account when employees contribute just 5%. Fully paid long term disability insurance, guaranteed-issue life insurance for new hires up to a volume of $150,000. Tuition waiver for full-time employees and their qualified dependents. Entrance in Tuition Exchange scholarship opportunities to pursue education at other institutions. Generous time off for administrative and staff employees."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/4212570": {
      "title": "Director of the Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning",
      "description": "Director of the Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. Purpose of Role Daemen University is seeking a collaborative and innovative Director of the Center for Excellence in Teaching & Learning (CETL). The Director provides leadership for faculty development and initiatives that strengthen teaching and learning across the University. Working with faculty, academic leadership, Instructional Design, and other campus partners, the Director develops programming and resources related to pedagogy, course design, student engagement, instructional technology, artificial intelligence, and effective teaching across all instructional modalities. The Director also supports faculty consultations, course development and redesign, and other instructional needs. About This Opportunity Lead the University's faculty development strategy in alignment with institutional priorities and emerging needs in higher education. Identify faculty development needs in collaboration with faculty, department chairs, academic deans, academic leadership, and campus partners. Develop and coordinate an annual calendar of professional development opportunities for full-time and adjunct faculty. Lead Sharpening the Edge of Excellence (SEE), Daemen's initiative to advance evidence-informed teaching practices and student learning. Plan and implement programs such as the Learning & Teaching Symposium, new faculty and adjunct orientations, workshops, teaching circles, mentoring initiatives, and scholarly presentations. Promote evidence-informed, student-centered, accessible, and innovative teaching practices. Support faculty engagement in the Scholarship of Teaching and Learning. Partner with Instructional Design to support effective course design and delivery across face-to-face, online, hybrid, and HyFlex modalities. Consult with faculty on pedagogy, course design, student engagement, instructional tools, and the responsible use of artificial intelligence. Develop and maintain faculty resources, training materials, guides, and communications. Assess CETL programming using participation data, faculty feedback, institutional information, and relevant research. Establish annual goals, manage the CETL budget and resources, and prepare reports on activities and outcomes. Coordinate new faculty onboarding each semester. Maintain a visible and accessible CETL presence and develop partnerships across the University. Serve on University committees, special projects, and events as assigned. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Relevant master's degree required; doctoral degree preferred. Minimum of three years of higher education teaching experience required; five or more years preferred. Experience with multiple instructional modalities, including online, hybrid, HyFlex, or blended learning. Experience designing and delivering faculty professional development or training. Demonstrated interest or experience in the Scholarship of Teaching and Learning. Experience in faculty development, teaching and learning, instructional design, or a comparable higher education role strongly preferred. Experience working with nontraditional students and diverse student populations preferred. Leadership experience preferred. Strong communication, collaboration, organizational, and project-management skills. General Physical Requirements Prolonged periods of sitting at a desk and/or working on a computer. Ability to move around the office to access filing cabinets, office machinery, etc. Ability (manual dexterity) to operate standard office equipment such as computers, telephones, photocopiers, etc. May need to walk across campus to deliver materials or support events in various locations. Must be able to lift up to 10 pounds at times. Total Compensation Daemen University offers a robust total compensation package that includes: Health insurance with an option of two plans: an HSA plan with the deductible funded by employer HSA contributions, or a copay plan. Dental insurance through the Guardian network. Vision insurance through the Guardian network, and an option between the VSP or Davis plans. An 8% employer contribution to the retirement savings account when employees contribute just 5%. Fully paid long term disability insurance, guaranteed-issue life insurance for new hires up to a volume of $150,000. Tuition waiver for full-time employees and their qualified dependents. Entrance in Tuition Exchange scholarship opportunities to pursue education at other institutions. Generous time off for administrative and staff employees."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/4229021": {
      "title": "DPT Program Director",
      "description": "DPT Program Director. Daemen University. Daemen University invites applications for the position of Doctor of Physical Therapy Program Director. This is a full-time, 12-month, tenure track faculty position in the Physical therapy Department with an immediate negotiable start date, but no later than starting September 01, 2027. Responsibilities and Duties: The Doctor of Physical Therapy Program director provides academic, administrative, and strategic leadership for the DPT program and is responsible for advancing program quality, effectiveness, and continued compliance with CAPTE accreditation standards. Essential responsibilities include: Provide strategic and operational leadership for the DPT program, faculty, staff, and students in alignment with the mission, goals and priorities of the program and University. Lead ongoing program assessment, strategic planning and continuous quality improvement using student, faculty, graduate, curricula, accreditation, and other program outcome data. Provide leadership for curriculum development, implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement to ensure contemporary, evidence-based physical therapist education and preparation for professional practice. Maintain effective communication and collaborative relationships with faculty, students, University leadership and departments, clinical education partners, advisory groups, community partners, alumni, and other internal and external stakeholders. Lead, support, mentor, and evaluate program faculty and promote faculty professional development, scholarly activity, teaching effectiveness, and professional engagement. Foster a collaborative and inclusive academic environment that supports student and faculty success, belonging, professionalism, and equitable educational practices. Manage program personnel and resources effectively, including participation in faculty recruitment, workload planning, performance management, conflict resolution, and organizational change. Provide leadership and appropriate oversight of the program's fiscal resources, including annual and long-range budget planning, resource allocation, personal expenditures, equipment, technology, supplies, facilities, and other resources necessary to support program quality and sustainability. Participate meaningfully in institutional decision-making regarding program enrollment and cohort size, tuition and program fees, financial resources, staffing, facilities, and other matters affecting the academic integrity and long-term viability of the DPT program. Assess program resource needs and effectively advocate for additional faculty, staff, financial, technological, physical, and educational resources when necessary to achieve program goals and expected outcomes. Maintain knowledge of CAPTE accreditation requirements and provide leadership to ensure ongoing program compliance with accreditation standards, institutional policies, applicable regulatory requirements, and expectations of contemporary physical therapist education. Represent and advocate for the DPT program within University governance and administration and externally within the physical therapy profession, higher education, healthcare community, and other professional and community organizations. Required Qualifications: Candidates must meet CAPTE requirements for service as a Doctor of Physical Therapy Program Director, including: Licensed physical therapist holding an active, unencumbered PT license in a United States jurisdiction and eligible to practice in accordance with applicable state requirements. Earned academic doctoral degree in a related field (e.g., PhD, EdD, DSc, or equivalent academic doctorate). Academic qualifications and scholarly accomplishments appropriate for appointment at the rank of Associate Professor, Professor, Clinical Associate Professor, or Clinical Professor. Minimum of six years of full-time experience in higher education, including at least three years of full-time experience as a core faculty member in a CAPTE-accredited entry-level physical therapist education program. Demonstrated education, professional development, or experience in academic administration, management, and leadership. Demonstrated knowledge and experience in educational theory and methodology, instructional design, student evaluation, and educational outcome assessment. Experience with fiscal management, budgeting, resource allocation, and program planning. Experience or formal preparation in program evaluation, assessment, curriculum development, and continuous quality improvement. Knowledge of CAPTE accreditation standards and processes and experience working with accreditation and/or regulatory requirements. Demonstrated experience participating in institutional governance and working collaboratively within a higher education environment. Total Compensation Daemen University offers a robust total compensation package that includes: Health insurance with an option of two plans: an HSA plan with the deductible funded by employer HSA contributions, or a copay plan. Dental insurance through the Guardian network. Vision insurance through the Guardian network, and an option between the VSP or Davis plans. An 8% employer contribution to the retirement savings account when employees contribute just 5%. Fully paid long term disability insurance and guaranteed-issue life insurance for new hires up to a volume of $150,000. Tuition waiver for full-time employees and their qualified dependents. Entrance in Tuition Exchange scholarship opportunities to pursue education at other institution. Within the Scott Bieler College of Health Professions, Daemen University offers an entry level Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) degree program. The DPT curriculum is a 6-year, 3+3 program. Students may apply to the Bachelor of Science in Natural Science/DPT program as freshmen or transfers. Students already possessing a baccalaureate degree may apply directly to the professional phase of the curriculum. The Physical Therapy Department is currently comprised of 10 highly motivated core faculty members engaged in a variety of clinical, service, and scholarly activities with a common goal of providing an outstanding educational experience for our students. Daemen University provides a dynamic academic environment that fosters strong collaborative and interprofessional efforts within the University and local medical community. Our Scott Bieler College of Health Professions building provides state-of-the-art lecture and laboratory facilities dedicated to our PT students in all clinical practice settings. Our Center for Interprofessional Learning and Simulation was recently expanded to include a simulated ICU hospital room that includes a high-fidelity manikin and 10 point-of-care ultrasound units. Standardized patients are also regularly utilized across numerous courses in our curriculum. We recently opened a state-of-the-art rehabilitation facility, the Kennedy Institute for Mobility Innovation & Technology (KIMIT) which offers access to leading robotic rehabilitation devices and assistive technology to restore motion and function following a range of injuries and illnesses. This center is Western New York's most comprehensive advanced rehabilitation facility of its kind in the region. Daemen University is a small private institution offering Baccalaureate, Masters, clinical and academic Doctoral degrees, in a wide variety of professional and liberal arts programs. Daemen University is a dynamic institution with over 2,700 full and part-time students and exhibits a rich history in physical therapy education. Notified of its latest reaccreditation from the Commission on Accreditation in Physical Therapy Education (CAPTE) in November 2017, the PT program has been continuously accredited by CAPTE since 1977. Located on a scenic suburban campus in Western New York, the local area offers numerous community festivals, a vibrant arts scene, world-class architecture, and outstanding cuisine. Its proximity to Niagara Falls and an international border, along with low housing costs, makes Western New York a wonderful place to reside and recreate. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Excellent fringe benefits are available. Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications should be submitted to https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/ and should include a cover letter of application, statement of teaching philosophy, curriculum vitae, and three references with contact information. Daemen University is an AA/EOE and strongly encourages applications from women, veterans, people of color, individuals with disabilities and candidates who will contribute to and support the cultural fluency and diversity of our campus. We welcome you to visit our department's website for more information at: https://www.daemen.edu/academics/scott-bieler-college-health-professions/physical-therapy"
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/4187035": {
      "title": "First Year Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "First Year Admissions Counselor. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. Purpose of Role The Admissions Counselor represents Daemen University to prospective students and organizations and works to increase inquiries and convert applications into enrolled students. The successful admissions counselor exhibits superior customer service skills and professionalism throughout daily interactions and communications with students including interviews, phone calls, emails and information sessions. The counselor creates and implements recruitment strategies to reach prospective students through events, referrals, online and print communications, and outreaches to businesses and organizations About This Opportunity Discuss Daemen University programs and services accurately to prospective students and families. Travel to and from recruitment events; engage in key stakeholders in a positive, proactive, and engaging manner. Complete weekly activity report to include documentation of recruitment/ outreach activities and student appointments. Ability to work on a registration deadline, strive towards college-wide enrollment goals and use outstanding customer service to recruit students to the Universities programs. Review applications and make enrollment decisions based on Daemen's admission standards for first year, transfer, and graduate student candidates. Role may specialize in specifically in first year, transfer, or graduate. Familiarity with engaging each type of student candidate preferred. Utilize phone, email, and mail to communicate with prospective students in a timely manner, providing superior student service. Work with prospective students to garner completed application files prior to enrollment and efforts to increase retention. Become familiar with working territory and demographics of cities/towns in that area to best reach the student population for Daemen University. Collaborate with our growing alumni network to develop new student/professional networks, garner student referrals. Under the direction of the Director, participate in the events prior, during, and after each term such as information sessions, orientations, registration events and graduation. Ability to work independently, and to arrange information sessions, set appointments and promote the University in a positive manner. Ability to follow the expectation of treating fellow employees, students and the institution's guests with civility, and to refrain from activities that disrupt the efficient functioning of the University. Ability to follow directions and complete tasks accurately as well as accept supervisory input and constructive criticism. Must be able to lift 25 lbs. and stand for an extended period f time as part of travel and college fair recruitment. Perform other duties as needed Required Qualifications The Admissions Counselor must have a minimum of an earned Bachelor's Degree from a regionally accredited institution and a working knowledge of college purpose and function. The Admissions Counselor must demonstrate an ability to work independently as well as collaboratively with team members, faculty, students, alumni, administrators and staff. A flexible work schedule that will include days, evenings, and some weekends is required. Travel, valid driver's license and access to a vehicle are required. Total Compensation Daemen University offers a robust total compensation package that includes: Health insurance with an option of two plans: an HSA plan with the deductible funded by employer HSA contributions, or a copay plan. Dental insurance through the Guardian network. Vision insurance through the Guardian network, and an option between the VSP or Davis plans. An 8% employer contribution to the retirement savings account when employees contribute just 5%. Fully paid long term disability insurance, guaranteed-issue life insurance for new hires up to a volume of $150,000. Tuition waiver for full-time employees and their qualified dependents. Entrance in Tuition Exchange scholarship opportunities to pursue education at other institutions. Generous time off for administrative and staff employees."
