    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/4189401": {
      "title": "Instructional Designer",
      "description": "Instructional Designer. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student-centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, and civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. Purpose of Role An Instructional Designer at Daemen University plays a crucial role in enhancing the educational experience for both students and faculty. An Instructional Designer is essential for creating a dynamic and effective learning environment. They support our faculty as they create courses and programs that are well-designed, technology-enhanced, and accessible. This is an on-campus position. About This Opportunity Joining our Instructional Design team within the Office of the Vice Provost; Institutional Effectiveness and Academic Systems, an Instructional Designer will be responsible for the following: Responsibilities: Collaborate with faculty members in the development or conversion of courses for online, hybrid, and HyFlex learning modalities including the selection of appropriate technological, instructional, and assessment strategies while meeting the objectives of the course and honoring the academic goals of the institution Collaborate with Subject Matter Experts (SMEs) to identify, design, and develop course materials and assets using the Backward Design model while managing course development projects. Actively review existing courses and offer recommendations for continued refinement based on best practices in synchronous and asynchronous learning. Develop online lesson materials using faculty content, other instructional content, software applications (e.g. Articulate 360, Camtasia, etc), and our Learning Management System (Blackboard). Support faculty as needed in the use of instructional technology in developing courses. Aid faculty in preparing proposed and existing online courses for quality review using the Quality Matters (QM) Higher Ed Rubric. Provide timely formative feedback and assistance to faculty to enhance face-to-face, HyFlex, hybrid, and online courses. Recommend innovative design, format, and/or technological changes to further engage learners. Effectively lead instructional workshops and presentations on innovative strategies to enhance teaching and learning. Collaborate with faculty on developing engaging content (e.g., video, audio, and/or interactive). Manage project timelines for instructional design projects. Stay informed about instructional technologies and curricular best practices. Assist with accessibility needs in keeping with the Americans with Disabilities Act. Support and stay informed in the area of Universal Design for Learning. Serve on the Quality in Online Education Committee (QOnEc). Take initiative to create user guides, tutorials, and other resources as \"on-demand\" references for faculty and staff. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Instructional Design, Educational Technology, or related disciplines. Experience with course design aimed at actively engaging students and meeting the needs of adult learners preferred. Experience with conducting online course reviews and communicating results and recommendations. Familiarity with common instructional design principles and best practices (e.g., ADDIE, Integrated or Backwards Design, formative feedback, etc.) Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to work collaboratively and independently as needed. Proficiency with Content or Learning Management Systems (e.g. Blackboard) Expertise in MS Office and Google Drive. Experience working on project teams to accomplish tasks and milestones as delineated and expected. Preferred Qualifications: Masters degree in Instructional Design, Educational Technologies, or related disciplines. Experience in higher education with a fluency in pedagogical modalities. Experience teaching in an online, hybrid, or HyFlex experience. Experience as a functional administrator for an LMS system including proficiency in their administration, customization, and support preferably Anthology Blackboard Ultra. Experience with the Quality Matters (QM) Higher Education Rubric. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States. The University does not provide visa sponsorship for this position. Total Compensation Daemen University offers a robust total compensation package that includes: Health insurance with an option of two plans: an HSA plan with the deductible partially funded by employer HSA contributions, or a copay plan. Dental insurance through the Guardian network. Vision insurance through the Guardian network, and an option between the VSP or Davis plans. An 8% employer contribution to the retirement savings account when employees contribute just 5%. Fully paid long term disability insurance, guaranteed-issue life insurance for new hires up to a volume of $150,000. Tuition waiver for full-time employees and their qualified dependents. Entrance in Tuition Exchange scholarship opportunities to pursue education at other institutions. Generous time off for administrative and staff employees."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/3114524": {
      "title": "Maintenance Mechanic 1 (1st Shift)",
      "description": "Maintenance Mechanic 1 (1st Shift). Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. Purpose of Role Under supervision, the Maintenance Mechanic 1 performs all general building maintenance repairs. Has knowledge in basic electrical, plumbing and heating adequate to make minor improvements and replacements. Preferred to have additional basic knowledge in carpentry, masonry, and vehicle maintenance. About This Opportunity Joining our Maintenance team, the Maintenance Mechanic will be responsible for the following: Maintain and replace sinks, toilets, urinals, and drinking fountains. Perform repairs to furniture. Repair and/or replace/install new ceilings and flooring. Repair and installation of lighting fixtures, light switches, receptacles, and smoke detectors. Perform various patching, painting, and staining tasks. Minor drywall repairs. Adjust and make repairs to door hardware including closures and exit devices. Perform preventative maintenance on mechanical equipment to include lubrication of pumps and motors, change filters and belts. Adjust, minor repairs and preventative maintenance to boilers and ventilation systems. Perform minor masonry repairs and concrete work. Moving furniture, hanging pictures, banners, and other signage. Assembling, repairing chairs, desks, shelving units, etc. Maintain university vehicles and equipment. Handle/assist with university event set ups and breakdowns. Inspect buildings, facilities, and equipment to ascertain required repairs and make recommendations to supervisor. Basic computer skills to operate software for automation system - view only. Considered essential personnel - which means that this position may be needed at times when the University is closed or in an emergency as determined by supervisor. Any other duties which may be assigned by the Assistant Directors or Director. Shift: 7am - 3:30pm Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma or GED. A minimum of 5 years of experience in building maintenance in a similar situation. Valid New York State driver's license that satisfies both the University and insurance company underwriting rules and regulations for driving a university owned motor vehicle. Ability to drive a university vehicle for the purpose of performing university business on a regular basis. Position is considered essential personnel and is required to work overtime and weekend as required by inclement weather or scheduled campus event as directed by supervision. Ability to read, write, speak and understand English. Ability to follow department Uniform Policy. Willingness to work some Saturdays as part of a Saturday rotation of all maintenance mechanics. Basic knowledge and provision of personal hand tools for building trades sufficient to perform minor repairs in carpentry, plumbing and electrical. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: General knowledge of building maintenance. General knowledge of carpentry, plumbing, electrical and heating repairs. General knowledge of construction principles. Good mechanical abilities Knowledge of proper use and maintenance of hand and power tools related to job functions, with or without reasonable accommodations. Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing. Ability to effectively as an individual or within a team as well as with diverse groups. Ability to work overtime to respond to emergencies. Ability to work effectively in a service-oriented environment, subject to frequently changing priorities. Problem solving skills and sound judgment in a technical environment. Basic computer skills necessary to use a work order system. Ability to work nights, weekends, and evenings as necessary. Adhere to safety procedures in the performance of job and be conscious of security issues involved in daily routine. Ability to perform all above essential job functions for a minimum of an eight-hour shift, with one-half hour unpaid meal break, without significant risk of serious injury. Ability to learn and perform all essential job functions accurately, with minimal direct supervision, within two weeks after the employee begins work. Attention to detail and a positive attitude. Starting from $18/hr, commensurate with experience. Total Compensation Daemen University offers a robust total compensation package that includes: Health insurance with an option of two plans: an HSA plan with the deductible funded by employer HSA contributions, or a copay plan. Dental insurance through the Guardian network. Vision insurance through the Guardian network, and an option between the VSP or Davis plans. An 8% employer contribution to the retirement savings account when employees contribute just 5%. Fully paid long term disability insurance, guaranteed-issue life insurance for new hires up to a volume of $150,000. Tuition waiver for full-time employees and their qualified dependents. Entrance in Tuition Exchange scholarship opportunities to pursue education at other institutions. Generous time off for administrative and staff employees. Daemen University strongly encourages all campus community members to get vaccinated for COVID-19, including a booster vaccine."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/3016178": {
      "title": "Physics Laboratory Instructor",
      "description": "Physics Laboratory Instructor. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. About This Opportunity Joining our Natural Sciences team, the Physics Laboratory Instructor will be responsible for the following: PHY 201L (General Physics I laboratory); 1 Credit Hour(s) PHY 201L: Topics focus on scientific reasoning and experimental design while exploring concepts of velocity, acceleration, forces, and vectors. Experience with \"active learning\" in both an online and face to face modality. Demonstrates strong interpersonal and communication skills, verbal and written, necessary to interact effectively with all university constituents. Strong time management/organizational skills. Demonstrated ability to work with students, faculty, staff, and all university administration. Demonstrated commitment to working with diverse populations. Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching. $1025 per class taught. Part-Time In-person Laboratory Instructor, fall semester. Instructor will teach a 2-contact hour, 1 credit hour laboratory. Instructor may teach more than one section. Please submit letter of interest, curriculum vitae, transcripts (official or unofficial) and contact information for two (2) references to application Required Qualifications Master's degree in Physics or related fields; previous experience teaching college-level science preferred. Daemen University strongly encourages all campus community members to get vaccinated for COVID-19, including a booster vaccine."
    },
    "https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/4212649": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Biology. Daemen University. Daemen University is a dynamic, independent, liberal arts institution committed to excellence in student centered learning. The University places special emphasis on preparing students for excellence in professional life, civic engagement, and on instilling and understanding that learning is an exciting lifelong journey. Students are encouraged to be creative, innovative, ethically minded leaders for an ever-changing, diverse, and interconnected world. The Mission of Daemen University is to prepare students for life and leadership in an increasingly diverse and complex world through the integration of education and professional preparation. Daemen University is going beyond instrumental needs to foster the development of individuals who are dedicated to the health and well-being of local and global communities. Tenure Track Professor of Biology The Natural Sciences and Mathematics department at Daemen University invites applications for a tenure track assistant professor of biology teaching position starting Fall 2027. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching 21 credits of lectures and laboratories primarily in the areas of General Biology, Microbiology, and Immunology to primarily allied-health students. Additional courses in the candidate's area of expertise may also be required. Tenure track faculty will also be responsible for mentoring undergraduate research students and conducting their own research leading to publication in peer-reviewed journals. All applicants must be willing and able to teach in both face-to-face and online modalities. Minimum Qualifications: Education PhD in Biology, Microbiology, or a related discipline required. Knowledge and Skills Experience with active learning in a face-to-face modality, preferably at smaller institutions. Demonstrates analytical and organizational skills necessary to plan, implement, and evaluate educational activities to assure compliance with established goals and objectives. Demonstrates strong interpersonal and communication skills, verbal and written, necessary to interact effectively with all university constituents. Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate education and mentoring. Ability to develop and maintain an active research program involving undergraduate students. Total Compensation Daemen University offers a robust total compensation package that includes: Health insurance with an option of two plans: an HSA plan with the deductible funded by employer HSA contributions, or a copay plan. Dental insurance through the Guardian network. Vision insurance through the Guardian network, and an option between the VSP or Davis plans. An 8% employer contribution to the retirement savings account when employees contribute just 5%. Fully paid long term disability insurance, guaranteed-issue life insurance for new hires up to a volume of $150,000. Tuition waiver for full-time employees and their qualified dependents. Entrance in Tuition Exchange scholarship opportunities to pursue education at other institutions. Generous time off for administrative and staff employees. For consideration, submit a letter of interest, resume, and references to https://daemen.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . Review of applicants begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Daemen University is an AA/EOE and strongly encourages applications from women, veterans, people of color, individuals with disabilities and candidates who will contribute to and support the cultural fluency and diversity of our campus."
    }
  },
